From ac1aa13974d6cf2bcb0d360445b1ebe973ef5c29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sukrit Jaidee <45908411+SukritJaAIproject@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:23:21 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/18] feat(desktop): read the Overview's edition numbers from
 the bundled benchmark

The two desktop editions ship the same UI bundle and differ only in
data/summary.json and model weights, yet the Overview was built from literals
and research constants, so both editions read almost the same.

- edition-benchmark.ts: held-out fault mix from leaderboard byFamily counts,
  the research label profile matching this edition's labels, and whether the
  research panel's model set (41ded2cdd5c2ba3f) is this edition's - decided by
  the sidecar artifact id, else by an exact baseline-arm leaderboard match.
- Fault-mix donut shows this edition's held-out set (7 families / 1,326 for
  v4, 6 / 957 for the 2026-09-12 snapshot) with a toggle to the research
  full-fleet mix, now labelled as research on ISO-reviewed labels.
- Research panel opens on the edition's own label profile, marks it, and says
  which model set it rescored; stat-row shares are computed.
- Hero chips, station subtitles and the fault-guide count come from the
  bundle; "31 regression checks" (stale) is gone.
- fault-catalog.ts: add NO_POWER_DELIVERED - v1.2.x rendered its largest
  family as "Unclassified AI anomaly" - plus a reason hint for it.
- vitest.config.ts: oxc jsx automatic. tsconfig keeps jsx:preserve for Next
  and Vite 8 has no esbuild, so no .tsx could be imported in a test; this also
  revives the MaximoWorkOrders suite that failed to load. 263/263 pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
